## Analysis

The problem asks me to prove the **Pebbling Number Conjecture** (Graham's conjecture): for connected graphs $G$ and $H$,

$$\pi(G \,\square\, H) \leq \pi(G) \cdot \pi(H),$$

where $\pi(\cdot)$ denotes the pebbling number and $\square$ denotes the Cartesian product of graphs.

